From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 18:35:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] sweet-a6xx: keep ZAP metadata in the GPU pool

TrustZone reads INIT_IMAGE metadata from ordinary non-secure DRAM. The
bare-metal shim authenticates from the GPU pool, while the kernel used the
later pil_gpu_region destination and failed with rc 1, r1 0x82.

Keep the .mdt metadata at A6_OFF_ZAP_META in the pool. PAS_IS_SUPPORTED is
already issued before INIT_IMAGE, and .b02 remains the later MEM_SETUP
destination.
---
 bsd/dev/sweet_a6xx.c | 21 +++++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

diff --git a/bsd/dev/sweet_a6xx.c b/bsd/dev/sweet_a6xx.c
--- a/bsd/dev/sweet_a6xx.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/sweet_a6xx.c
@@ -749,16 +749,17 @@ zap_load(struct a6_gpu *g)
 	/*
-	 * SCM_PIL(INIT_IMAGE) takes a 32-bit physical address on this platform. The
-	 * pool sits above 4 GiB (0x184a00000 here), so passing pool+A6_OFF_ZAP_META
-	 * truncates and TrustZone rejects the image with rc 1, r1 0x82 - which is
-	 * exactly what the kernel logged while bare-metal shim-rmx (low memory)
-	 * authenticated the same blob. Put the metadata in the low zap region
-	 * instead (8 KB); TZ copies it during INIT_IMAGE, before .b02 is written
-	 * over the same region below.
+	 * TrustZone reads the metadata from ordinary non-secure DRAM. Keep it in
+	 * the GPU pool, matching the bare-metal shim's ZAP_META location; the
+	 * pil_gpu_region is the later firmware segment destination.
 	 */
-	uint64_t meta_pa = zap_region;
+	uint64_t meta_pa = a6_pool_pa(g, A6_OFF_ZAP_META);
 	a6_write(meta_pa, mdt, mlen);
-	a6_log("zap: meta %llx len %u (pool %llx low)\n", (unsigned long long)meta_pa,
-	    mlen, (unsigned long long)a6_pool_pa(g, A6_OFF_ZAP_META));
+	a6_log("zap: meta %llx len %u (pool)\n", (unsigned long long)meta_pa, mlen);
+	int64_t sup = scm(7, 1, PAS_GPU, 0, 0, &r1);
+	a6_log("zap: pas supported(13) rc %lld r1 %llx\n",
+	    (long long)sup, (unsigned long long)r1);
+	if (sup || r1) {
+		return -1;
+	}
 	int64_t rc = scm(1, 2 | (2u << 6), PAS_GPU, meta_pa, 0, &r1);
 	if (rc || r1) {
 		a6_log("zap: init image rc %lld r1 %llx\n", (long long)rc, (unsigned long long)r1);
-- 
